{"content":[{"c":["ELAM (P",{"c":["erson"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Firstborn son of Shem and a grandson of Noah (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.10.22","r":"Gen.10.22","rawR":"Gen.10.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.10.22","value":"Gen.10.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 10:22"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.1.17","r":"1Chr.1.17","rawR":"1Chr.1.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.1.17","value":"1Chr.1.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 1:17"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Benjamite and the son of Shashak (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.8.24","r":"1Chr.8.24","rawR":"1Chr.8.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.8.24","value":"1Chr.8.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 8:24"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Korahite Levite and the fifth son of Kore from the house of Asaph (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.26.3","r":"1Chr.26.3","rawR":"1Chr.26.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.26.3","value":"1Chr.26.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 26:3"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Forefather of 1,254 descendants who returned with Zerubbabel to Judah following the exile (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.2.7","r":"Ezra.2.7","rawR":"Ezra.2.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.2.7","value":"Ezra.2.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 2:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.7.12","r":"Neh.7.12","rawR":"Neh.7.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.7.12","value":"Neh.7.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 7:12"},"). Later, 71 members of Elam’s house accompanied Ezra back to Palestine during the reign of King Artaxerxes I of Persia (464–424 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.8.7","r":"Ezra.8.7","rawR":"Ezra.8.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.8.7","value":"Ezra.8.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 8:7"},"). In postexilic Judah, Shecaniah, Elam’s descendant, urged Ezra to command the sons of Israel to divorce their foreign wives (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.10.2","r":"Ezra.10.2","rawR":"Ezra.10.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.10.2","value":"Ezra.10.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:2"},"); a number from Elam’s house eventually did so (v ",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.10.26","r":"Ezra.10.26","rawR":"Ezra.10.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.10.26","value":"Ezra.10.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"26"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["5. Another forefather of 1,254 descendants who returned with Zerubbabel to Judah (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.2.31","r":"Ezra.2.31","rawR":"Ezra.2.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.2.31","value":"Ezra.2.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 2:31"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.7.34","r":"Neh.7.34","rawR":"Neh.7.34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.7.34","value":"Neh.7.34"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 7:34"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["6. One of the chiefs of Israel who set his seal on Ezra’s covenant (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.10.14","r":"Neh.10.14","rawR":"Neh.10.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.10.14","value":"Neh.10.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 10:14"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["7. One of the priestly musicians who performed at the dedication of the Jerusalem wall (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.42","r":"Neh.12.42","rawR":"Neh.12.42","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.42","value":"Neh.12.42"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:42"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"ElamPerson","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 10:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.10.22","rawQueryValue":"Gen.10.22","sourceRefExact":"Gen.10.22"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 1:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.1.17","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.1.17","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.1.17"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 8:24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.8.24","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.8.24","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.8.24"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 26:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.26.3","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.26.3","sourceR